Vendored DCS World scripting-API schema
========================================

These files are a frozen, unmodified copy of the `dcs-world-schema` project,
used by VEAF-Mission-Creation-Tools as the reference set of DCS scripting-API
functions (see the `audit-dcs-mocks` command) and, optionally, as an IDE
reference (EmmyLua/LuaLS) for contributors writing VEAF Lua.

Source:      https://github.com/YoloWingPixie/dcs-world-schema
Release tag: v0.3.5
Fetch date:  2026-06-27
License:     MIT (see the LICENSE file alongside)

Vendored artifacts
------------------
- dcs-world-api-schema.json  -- machine-readable API description (audit reference)
- dcs-world-api.lua          -- EmmyLua annotations for LuaLS autocomplete (.luarc.json)

Known defect in this copy -- country names
------------------------------------------
Do not read country names from `types["country.name"]` in dcs-world-api-schema.json.
Measured against v0.3.5 on 2026-09-19: DCS has no country at id 14, and that table
renumbers its names sequentially across the hole, so every country from id 14 onward
carries the name of the one below it -- 78 of the 92 entries are wrong, and New
Zealand (id 92) is missing from it entirely.

`types["country.id"]` is correct and reproduces the hole faithfully. The repository's
own table, veaf_libs/data/dcs-countries.yaml, is the source of truth for country ids
and is what every VMCT lookup uses; nothing here reads the broken table.

Reported upstream as YoloWingPixie/dcs-world-schema#22. Re-check at the next bump
and drop this section once it is fixed; test/python/test_vendored_schema_country_ids.py
guards the id table meanwhile.

Updating
--------
Updating these files is an explicit bump commit: re-download the assets from a
newer release tag, replace the files, and update the "Release tag" / "Fetch date"
fields above. Drift detection of this vendored copy is handled by the
VENDORED-DRIFT-WATCH lot.
